  "reference_answer_text": "①",
  "reference_solution": "[정답] ①\n\n[해설]\n$\\frac{\\cos \\theta}{\\tan \\theta} + \\sin \\theta = \\sqrt{3}$에서\n$\\frac{\\cos^{2} \\theta}{\\sin \\theta} + \\sin \\theta$$= \\frac{\\cos^{2} \\theta + \\sin^{2} \\theta}{\\sin \\theta}$\n$= \\frac{1}{\\sin \\theta} = \\sqrt{3}$\n$\\sin \\theta = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}$이다.\n$\\sin^{2} \\theta + \\cos^{2} \\theta = 1$이므로\n$\\frac{1}{3} + \\cos^{2} \\theta = 1$, $\\cos^{2} \\theta = \\frac{2}{3}$\n$\\frac{\\pi}{2} < \\theta < \\pi$에서 $\\cos \\theta < 0$이다.\n따라서 $\\cos \\theta = - \\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{3}$\n",
  "problem_text": "$\\frac{\\pi}{2} < \\theta < \\pi$인 $\\theta$에 대하여 $\\frac{\\cos \\theta}{\\tan \\theta} + \\sin \\theta = \\sqrt{3}$일 때, $\\cos \\theta$의 값은?\n① $- \\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{3}$\t② $- \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}$\t③ $- \\frac{1}{3}$\n④ $\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}$\t⑤ $\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{3}$\n",
